,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/deployments","created_at":"2026-08-05T16:00:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T17:31:44Z","pushed_at":"2026-09-23T18:02:56Z","git_url":"git://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF","homepage":"http://agentfield.ai/","size":196153,"stargazers_count":116,"watchers_count":116,"language":"Go","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":14,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":141,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["agent-fleet","agent-harness","agentfield","agentic-coding","ai","ai-coding","cli-agent","coding-agent","coding-agents","coding-assistant","coding-cli","coding-harness","developer-tools","harness","harness-engineering","llm","open-models","open-source-models","software-factory","terminal-agent"],"visibility":"public","forks":14,"open_issues":141,"watchers":116,"default_branch":"dev","permissions":{"admin":true,"maintain":true,"push":true,"triage":true,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pulls/1224","html_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pull/1224","diff_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pull/1224.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pull/1224.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"A design page only. No code changes. The owner answered both of its questions on 2026-09-20, so it is settled rather than proposed and three cells follow it.\n\n## The rule\n\nClosing a window never ends work and never loses it. Work is always in one of three conditions the screen names: running, interrupted, or settled. While the engine is alive a run keeps running. When nothing is driving it, it is interrupted, never failed, and everything it did is kept. On the next launch the person is asked once and `enter` continues. Nothing restarts silently, and the five-minute tick never continues a run.\n\n## What it records as true today\n\n- A live run does not count as work, so the engine retires its conversation at 30 minutes, mid-run.\n- A run's context belongs to the turn that proposed it, not to the conversation.\n- On reopen an unsettled run row is stamped failed and stopped, over a store that holds every row.\n- The supervisor can already release dead claims and carry on from a store. Nothing calls it on reopen.\n\n## The owner's answers\n\nBoth yes, in his own words, quoted at the foot of the page:\n\n> 1. `interrupted` is the state word. Yes.\n> 2. Continuing always asks first, and the five-minute tick never continues a run on its own. Yes.\n>\n> The design is settled on those two points. Build it as written.\n\nSo `interrupted` joins running, finishing, done, incomplete and your call, and means only \"nothing is driving this\". The fourth row in the order of work, the tick continuing a run on its own, is refused by that second answer. It is written down as refused rather than merely unbuilt.\n\n## The three cells\n\n| # | Cell | Size | New words |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| a | a live run counts as work; the run's context is the conversation's; the engine stays while a run lives | S | none |\n| b | on reopen, an unsettled run reads `interrupted` from the store's own state, never failed and stopped | S | `interrupted` |\n| c | the card, and continue through the existing supervisor on the existing store | M | none beyond b |\n\nThe order is not arbitrary. Cell b reads a condition that cell a is what makes truthful, and cell c draws the word cell b introduces.\n\nTwo acceptance notes are now on the page beside that table, because they are the parts most likely to be dropped under time pressure. A cell that has to end an engine ends it by the process id recorded when it was launched, confirmed by reading that process's own executable, never by matching a pattern against a command line and never by signalling a group. And cell b carries the manual in both directions: the new word has to reach the pages, and the page that today tells a person their run ended when codeaf closed has to be found and corrected in the same change, because a page that names a word while denying the thing around it satisfies every gate and still lies.\n\n## Proof\n\nDocs only, so the light gate is the level. On Spark, plain ssh, a detached tree of head `c97770f35`. Exit codes read directly.\n\n| Step | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `go build ./...` | exit 0 |\n| `make test-laws` | exit 0 |\n| `internal/manual`, `internal/namelaw` | ok |\n| `make changelog-check` | exit 0 |\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1224/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1224/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":31500788231,"node_id":"MIE_lADOTu5AHM8AAAABSQJF088AAAAHVZfiBw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/events/31500788231","actor":{"login":"santoshkumarradha","id":29346072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MzQ2MDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29346072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha","html_url":"https://github.com/santoshkumarradha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"milestoned","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2026-09-21T02:34:49Z","milestone":{"title":"Reliable agent"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":315007882